@startuml gestor_tareas_sequence
' Sequence diagram for Task Manager Application

actor User
participant UI as "User Interface"
participant Controller
participant Service
participant DB as "Database"

== Register Client ==
User -> UI: Enter client data
UI -> Controller: submitClient(data)
Controller -> Service: validateAndRegisterClient(data)
Service -> DB: checkDuplicateClient(data)
DB --> Service: not found
Service -> DB: saveClient(data)
DB --> Service: clientId
Service --> Controller: clientRegistered
Controller --> UI: showSuccess

== Register Category ==
User -> UI: Enter category data
UI -> Controller: submitCategory(data)
Controller -> Service: validateAndRegisterCategory(data)
Service -> DB: checkDuplicateCategory(data)
DB --> Service: not found
Service -> DB: saveCategory(data)
DB --> Service: categoryId
Service --> Controller: categoryRegistered
Controller --> UI: showSuccess

== Register Task ==
User -> UI: Enter task data
UI -> Controller: submitTask(data)
Controller -> Service: validateAndRegisterTask(data)
Service -> DB: saveTask(data)
DB --> Service: taskId
Service --> Controller: taskRegistered
Controller --> UI: showSuccess

== List Tasks by User and Status ==
User -> UI: Request tasks by status
UI -> Controller: getTasksByUserAndStatus(userId, status)
Controller -> Service: fetchTasks(userId, status)
Service -> DB: queryTasks(userId, status)
DB --> Service: tasksList
Service --> Controller: tasksList
Controller --> UI: displayTasks(tasksList)

@enduml
